      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-18T10:02:51Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): carry a flipped WCS X or Y into the posted program\n\nA setup's Flip X / Flip Y no longer refuses generation and the post.\nGeneration, verification and the stock simulation stay in the setup\nframe. The post mirrors each section that states PARAM WcsFlip: it\nnegates the flipped axis about the origin, swaps G2/G3 and G41/G42 when\none axis is flipped, and carries helix, canned cycles and probing.\nThe flip composes with machine-inverted axes. The travel check, the\nsetup sheet and the work envelope follow the posted sign.\n\nRefused by name: a flipped Z (#2474), a script that is not verified for\na mirror (#2475), flip plus rotation (#2476), turning, threading, live\ntool, ABC/tilt, EDM, wire, plasma, a modal origin across a change of\nflip, and a bad WcsFlip value.\n\nProcess change: yes (camcraft-mcp skill row).\n\nFixes #1649\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
