      "message": "feat(post): refuse probing in a flipped WCS by name\n\nThe maintainer's decision of 2026-11-18 keeps the meaning of a flip (the\nmachine control runs the flipped axis reversed) and refuses probing in a\nflipped setup. The probe's work-offset write is verified for an inverted\nmachine axis (#392), not for a mirrored work offset.\n\n- setup_wcs_flip: a probe operation in a flipped setup is refused at the\n  verification gate, with the flipped axes and the operation names.\n- post::wcs_flip: a flipped section with probe records is refused, so\n  each stream builder is covered.\n- MCP set_wcs_flip: the refused field also names the refused operations\n  of the setup (setup_post_problems).\n- WCS page: the note says that the control must run the axis reversed\n  and that probing does not post. The status line names a refusal in\n  place of \"mirrored\".\n\nRefs #1649\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
